\paragraph{Robustness across layer criteria.}
One concern is that threshold-dependent layer selection biases the comparison toward layers where HS probes happen to excel. Pure balanced-accuracy selection (a threshold-free metric) provides an independent check: at BA-selected layers, all 16 model-metric comparisons pass Holm-Bonferroni correction (\cref{tab:ba_layer_comparison}), with precision gains of +13.7 to +25.4pp. This refutes the circularity objection because the layer criterion does not optimize for the metrics used in the modality comparison. The result also confirms that the HS advantage is not confined to a narrow set of layers but persists across complementary selection criteria.

